{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And it shall be when you go, etc. And it shall, etc.</b> One needs to know why he repeated saying <b>וְהָיָה</b> a second time. Further, the entire verse seems superfluous, for these are the very same things stated in the first statement. And it may be explained according to two understandings: according to the opinion of Rabbi Eliezer, the word ״וְהָיָה״ etc. continues from what was said above, in this manner — ״וְהָיִיתָ לָּנוּ לְעֵינָיִם״, and it shall likewise be that when you go with us you will be reckoned at this level, and you will not be in the category of a lamp before the sun and moon as you said, according to the words of Rabbi Eliezer; and according to the words of Rabbi Joshua it intends that you will stand in this great status in our eyes." "And His saying <b>and it shall be that the good</b> etc. — meaning, according to the words of Rabbi Eliezer, who wished to go and return, he said to him: it is not proper to go and return, for I want you to be present at the time when HaShem gives the good to His people, so that we may do good to you with the finest portion of it, which would not be the case if you are not present at the time of the division of the land. And he was persuaded by this, except that after some time, when he saw that a decree had been issued upon Israel to remain in the wilderness forty years, he went to do his good deed — to convert the people of his city — and returned, and he was present at the time of HaShem's doing good to Israel, as Moses had said. And according to the words of Rabbi Joshua as well, the intention was to tell him that he should not consider himself a convert who would be at a lowly rank compared to the people, as implied by ״כִּי אִם אֶל אַרְצִי וְאֶל מוֹלַדְתִּי״ — which indicates that he wished to go to a place where he had acquaintances. Therefore he said: not so, but rather <b>and it shall be that the good which HaShem does for us shall be with us</b> — meaning, with all of us together, so that they would not reckon him at a rank lower than theirs. And further, that you will have the good and choicest portion among the portions, which is what ״וְהֵטַבְנוּ לָךְ״ means."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:31.101753407Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}